Description: Vibe engine: the language Vibe names, or the model's own choice
 The engine sent detect_language=true whenever Vibe's own settings named no language
 (or "automatic"). Vibe 3.3.5's server passes that field to its whisper-rs engine, whose
 full() detects the language and returns before any decoding when detect_language is
 set (server/crates/whisper-rs/src/full.rs), so every such dictation was answered with
 an empty text and said as "Vibe heard no speech in the recording.". Measured by the
 main session on a test machine with the real model: the same recording gave the right
 text with language=en and with neither field, and {"text":""} with detect_language=true.
 .
 The engine now sends a language only when Vibe's settings name one; with none, or
 automatic, it sends no language field, so the model detects the language and then
 transcribes (full.rs treats a missing, empty or "auto" language alike). An empty text
 for a recording is still said as before.
 .
 The test stand-in follows the server for these fields (detect_language answered with
 an empty text), the job test expects neither field when no language is set, and the
 plugin test reads the language from Vibe's store through the plugin interface: none,
 automatic, and Portuguese as the control.
Author: Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: no
